  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 6802.03 Laboratory Evaluation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 6802.03 Laboratory Evaluation.\n\n(a) The laboratory shall evaluate each manufacturer make and model of preliminary breath test device submitted in accordance with Saf-C 6802.02.\n\n(b) The evaluation shall include the following categories:\n\n(1) Analysis of a series of alcohol samples at known concentrations, to verify the accuracy and precision of the approved instrument as meeting the following criteria:\n\na. For known alcohol concentrations greater than 0.000 g/210L but less than or equal to\n\n0.050 g/210L:\n\n1. The accuracy of the readings shall deviate no more than +/- 0.003 g/210L from known alcohol concentrations; and\n\n2. The total precision range of the readings shall not exceed 0.005 g/210L;\n\nb. For known alcohol concentrations greater than 0.050 g/210L but less than or equal to 0.100 g/210L:\n\n1. The accuracy of the readings shall deviate no more than +/- 0.005 g/210L from known concentrations; and\n\n2. The total precision range of the readings shall not exceed 0.005 g/210L; and\n\nc. For known alcohol concentrations greater than 0.100 g/210L:\n\n1. The accuracy of the readings shall deviate no more than +/- 5% from known alcohol concentrations; and\n\n2. The total precision range of the readings shall not exceed 5% of the target value;\n\n(2) Ease of use in handling the device while performing a test;\n\n(3) Performance under normal and adverse ambient conditions; and\n\n(4) Effects of other substances or sources of energy that might interfere with the proper functioning of the device.\n\n(c) Each device evaluated in accordance with Saf-C 6802.03 shall meet or exceed the performance statements provided by the manufacturer.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at Chapter Heading for Saf-C 6800) #9685, eff 3-23-10; ss by #12518, eff 4-23-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c6800.html"
}
